 "thread": "Z2Wfd0LL1D4",
 "subject": "Changing label of legend and plotting both geom_tippoint and branches specifying colors.",
 "messages_listed": 2,
 "last_activity": "2017-08-15T09:28:02Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "iJeIATELAgAJ",
   "from": "Sebastian van Hal",
   "author": "14b9e51955638185",
   "date": "2017-08-08T11:24:48Z",
   "subject": "Changing label of legend and plotting both geom_tippoint and branches specifying colors.",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><div>Hi all - Please help.</div><div><br></div><div>I would like to plot branches by bootstrap values, change the title of the legend and then plot the tips by groups.</div><div><br></div><div>This successfully plot the tree using bootstrap values with legend title -&gt; bs</div><div>q&lt;-ggtree(tpre, aes(color=bs))+scale_colour_continuous(high=&quot;black&quot;, low=&#39;lightblue&#39;)+ theme(legend.position = &quot;bottom&quot;)<br></div><div><br></div><div>I have tried  but get legend.title, legend.text etc... but get error in element text or theme....</div><div>ggtree(midpoint.root(tpre), aes(color=bs))+scale_color_continuous(high=&quot;black&quot;, low=&#39;lightblue&#39;)+ theme(legend.position = &quot;bottom&quot;, title=element_text(&quot;bootstrap value&quot;, size=1, font=&quot;arial&quot;))</div><div><br></div><div>However when I try and combine the 2.</div><div><br></div><div>q %&lt;+% d + geom_tippoint(aes(color=as.factor(clusterID)), size=1)+scale_color_manual(values=c(&#39;1&#39;=&quot;red&quot;, &#39;2&#39;=&quot;yellow&quot;))<br></div><div><br></div><div><div>Scale for &#39;colour&#39; is already present. Adding another scale for &#39;colour&#39;, which will replace the existing scale.</div><div>Error: Continuous value supplied to discrete scale</div></div><div><br></div><div>The colour in q overrides the colour in d.</div><div><br></div><div>How can I do both?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks</div><div>Sebastian</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "fMncT46fCQAJ",
   "from": "Yu, Guangchuang",
   "author": "cec41188340e8212",
   "date": "2017-08-15T09:28:02Z",
   "subject": "Re: Changing label of legend and plotting both geom_tippoint and branches specifying colors.",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">The problem here is that you are trying to mapping two variable to color, and their will be appended as ggplot2 don’t allow you to have two color <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">aes</code> mapping. So you need to provide all the manual selected colors to <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">scale_color_continuous</code> instead of two separated sets.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">see an example in <a href=\"https://github.com/GuangchuangYu/ggtree/issues/78#issuecomment-252172314\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/GuangchuangYu/ggtree/issues/78%23issuecomment-252172314&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482693631000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1MF3mo0mBMdvpxto81ugT2\">https://github.com/GuangchuangYu/ggtree/issues/78#issuecomment-252172314</a>.</p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">On Tue, Aug 8, 2017 at 7:24 PM, Sebastian van Hal &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">vanh...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><div>Hi all - Please help.</div><div><br></div><div>I would like to plot branches by bootstrap values, change the title of the legend and then plot the tips by groups.</div><div><br></div><div>This successfully plot the tree using bootstrap values with legend title -&gt; bs</div><div>q&lt;-ggtree(tpre, aes(color=bs))+scale_colour_continuous(high=&quot;black&quot;, low=&#39;lightblue&#39;)+ theme(legend.position = &quot;bottom&quot;)<br></div><div><br></div><div>I have tried  but get legend.title, legend.text etc... but get error in element text or theme....</div><div>ggtree(midpoint.root(tpre), aes(color=bs))+scale_color_continuous(high=&quot;black&quot;, low=&#39;lightblue&#39;)+ theme(legend.position = &quot;bottom&quot;, title=element_text(&quot;bootstrap value&quot;, size=1, font=&quot;arial&quot;))</div><div><br></div><div>However when I try and combine the 2.</div><div><br></div><div>q %&lt;+% d + geom_tippoint(aes(color=as.factor(clusterID)), size=1)+scale_color_manual(values=c(&#39;1&#39;=&quot;red&quot;, &#39;2&#39;=&quot;yellow&quot;))<br></div><div><br></div><div><div>Scale for &#39;colour&#39; is already present. Adding another scale for &#39;colour&#39;, which will replace the existing scale.</div><div>Error: Continuous value supplied to discrete scale</div></div><div><br></div><div>The colour in q overrides the colour in d.</div><div><br></div><div>How can I do both?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks</div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div>Sebastian</div></font></span></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
